Cadencr backport: LSP exit status after shutdown

Upstream: microsoft/typescript-go 9977d6d38fcc78de8ae71770f3aa08256e6cc861
Issue:    https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/issues/64742
Origin:   https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/pull/64894 commit
          6e9659803b89d66d39631b1f0a762ff89f924360 (base 538671d3cc2dc1fa292dbb00185d3cdbef9aa73b)

The server.go added and removed lines equal that commit's. Adaptations to
the pinned source: paths drop the later tsc/ prefix, registerNotificationHandler
is a free function and handleShutdown has no closeAPISessions call at this
revision. The lifecycle tests are rewritten for this revision.

The pull request's second commit (9437ba19107a2b00b1dbf4b113e3e53afb37bc7b)
queues transport EOF behind dispatch. It is not applied: a handler awaiting a
client response, such as initialized, then never sees EOF and the server
never exits after its client closes stdin. The test
TestRunExitsOnTransportEOFWhileAwaitingClientResponse covers this case.

